comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-08T05:58:07.187Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status 2658-item title/metadata catalog and source ledger reviewed; current query epoch conditioned evidence confidence nearest pm-4k6b,pm-doxj,pm-hlf7ca,pm-92if,pm-rnpb. No individual owner for this experiment was found. Shared scorer/signal/packer baselines are prerequisites, not proof of this distinct mechanism. User requested individual planning records; this draft preserves the open cognitive-architecture decision gate and does not accept the ADR. Estimate is a one-day initial spike budget, not a delivery forecast."
body: "## Proposal and provenance\n\nStable algorithm slug: `epoch-conditioned-evidence-confidence`. Source: pm-4k6b note recorded 2026-08-08T22:00:52.713Z.\n\nContext relevance ledger (32): epoch-conditioned evidence confidence — discount a record's recorded measurements by whether the contract that produced them is still the contract that would be applied to read them.\n\nRecorded 2026-08-08. Extends the ledger; entries 1 through 31 stand.\n\nThe observation this is derived from. A correct refusal blocked the daily cut because the event predated the tag producer the gate reads, so the gate could not judge it and failed closed. Generalized on the roadmap as horizon AH. The relevance consequence is separate from the gate consequence and is what this entry captures: when the engine assembles context, it currently treats every recorded measurement as equally citable, whether it was written under the contracts in force today or under contracts that have since been replaced. An agent handed a number extracted from a record written three epochs ago will reason about it as though it were current, and the record gives it no way to know otherwise.\n\nWhat the signal computes. For each candidate item, determine the contract epoch under which its recorded evidence was written — the schema version, error-code catalog version, dependency-kind lexicon, and projection contract in force at its write timestamps — and compare that to the epoch in force now. The signal is a scalar in the unit interval: one when the item's evidence was written entirely under the current epoch, decaying toward a floor as the number of intervening contract changes that touch fields the item actually carries increases. Weighting is by touched field, not by elapsed time: an item whose only recorded fields are ones no contract change has altered is not discounted at all, however old it is, and an item written last week under a since-replaced projection is.\n\nWhy it is a relevance signal and not a validity check. It never asserts that old evidence is wrong. Old evidence is usually right, and the immutable record is the reason the project can be trusted at all. It asserts only that old evidence is less safe to quote without re-derivation, which is exactly the judgement a ranking engine exists to make. In assembly it should surface as an explainable per-signal component, so a bounded context can say why a fresher but less central item outranked an older, more central one.\n\nDegeneracy clauses, mandatory as for every entry in this ledger. On a corpus with exactly one contract epoch — any newly initialized workspace, and any project that has never changed a contract — the signal is identically one for every item and the ranking is byte-identical to the ranking without it. On a two-item corpus it is likewise identically one. The signal can only ever discount, never promote, so it cannot manufacture confidence in an item and cannot raise any ceiling; the worst case it can produce is a ranking that is uniformly one epoch conservative. If epoch metadata is unavailable for an item the signal returns one rather than a penalty, so an unmeasurable item is never demoted for being unmeasurable.\n\nRelationship to neighbouring entries. Distinct from (26) recurrence-conditioned retrieval priors, which conditions on how often a family recurs; this conditions on whether the vocabulary the evidence is written in still applies. Distinct from (23) citation-stable evidence addressing, which asks whether a citation still resolves; this asks whether a citation that does resolve still means what it said. It composes with (31), contract-seam staleness: (31) ranks the pair whose two sides were last edited in different changes, and this entry ranks the record written before either edit.\n\nCandidate only. It requires an epoch representation that does not exist yet, which is horizon AH's terminal answer, so it must be routed through that work and must not be weighted on the strength of one incident. Reference evidence: pm-h75tjh.\n\nScope clarification from individual-ownership review: pm-h75tjh owns a related measurement, read primitive or defect fix. It does not independently deliver this proposed ranking behavior. Reuse its evidence and public API; evaluate the additional behavior in this experiment.\n\n## Delivery boundary\n\nEvaluate this mechanism as a bounded public-SDK experiment before any production adoption. Use the existing scorer and packer contracts; no CLI-only behavior or new command noun. The historical catalog is design input, not evidence that this mechanism was implemented.\n\n## Experiment protocol\n\nFreeze a workspace/history revision and parameter manifest. Compare against the current deterministic SDK baseline using held-out judgments and negative controls. Report nDCG/action success, critical-evidence omission, latency p50/p95, peak memory, tokens per completed task, and rebuild cost separately. Include 3-item/minutes, real-shaped, 100k/1M-item, decades-long, and sparse/dense/imbalanced graph scenarios; smoke subsets may not claim scale acceptance. Bound candidate counts, graph expansions, elapsed time, and output size, with cancellation and completeness receipts. Record exact versus approximate behavior and approximation error; theoretical guarantees require their stated assumptions. Missing or untrusted evidence remains unknown, never inferred proof.\n\nPromotion requires a reproducible quality improvement on the held-out target population, no regression of existing exact invariants or mandatory gates, and a declared compute/token cost justified by that improvement. Reject or defer with the same immutable evidence if those conditions fail. No production default, adaptive learning, or data export is authorized by this planning item."
